---
import ToolLayout from '../../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import { toolBySlug } from '../../../lib/content/tools';
import { isLang } from '../../../lib/i18n';
if (!isLang(Astro.params.lang!)) return new Response(null, { status: 404 });
const lang = Astro.locals.lang; const fr = lang === 'fr'; const tool = toolBySlug('utm-builder')!;
const f = fr ? [['url', 'URL du site *', 'https://www.example.com/page'], ['utm_source', 'Source de campagne *', 'instagram, newsletter, google'], ['utm_medium', 'Média de campagne *', 'social, email, cpc'], ['utm_campaign', 'Nom de campagne', 'lancement_ete'], ['utm_term', 'Terme de campagne', 'mot-clé payant'], ['utm_content', 'Contenu de campagne', 'bouton_bio']] : [['url', 'Website URL *', 'https://www.example.com/page'], ['utm_source', 'Campaign source *', 'instagram, newsletter, google'], ['utm_medium', 'Campaign medium *', 'social, email, cpc'], ['utm_campaign', 'Campaign name', 'summer_launch'], ['utm_term', 'Campaign term', 'paid keyword'], ['utm_content', 'Campaign content', 'bio_button']];
---
<ToolLayout tool={tool}>
  <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6"><form class="card p-5 space-y-3" id="utm">{f.map(([k, l, ph]) => <div><label class="label">{l}</label><input name={k} class="input" placeholder={ph} type={k === 'url' ? 'url' : 'text'} /></div>)}</form>
    <div class="card p-5"><label class="label">{fr ? 'URL générée' : 'Generated URL'}</label><textarea id="out" rows="5" class="input font-mono text-sm" readonly></textarea><div class="mt-3 flex gap-2"><button type="button" class="btn-primary btn-sm" data-copy="#out"><i class="fa-regular fa-copy"></i>{fr ? 'Copier' : 'Copy'}</button><a id="open" href="#" target="_blank" class="btn-secondary btn-sm"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square"></i>{fr ? 'Ouvrir' : 'Open'}</a></div><p class="help mt-3" id="err"></p></div></div>
  <script>
    const form = document.getElementById('utm') as HTMLFormElement; const out = document.getElementById('out') as HTMLTextAreaElement; const open = document.getElementById('open') as HTMLAnchorElement;
    const render = () => { const fd = new FormData(form); let base = String(fd.get('url') || '').trim(); if (!base) { out.value = ''; return; } try { const u = new URL(/^https?:\/\//.test(base) ? base : 'https://' + base); for (const k of ['utm_source', 'utm_medium', 'utm_campaign', 'utm_term', 'utm_content']) { const v = String(fd.get(k) || '').trim(); if (v) u.searchParams.set(k, v); } out.value = u.toString(); open.href = u.toString(); document.getElementById('err')!.textContent = ''; } catch { document.getElementById('err')!.textContent = 'Invalid URL'; } };
    form.addEventListener('input', render);
  </script>
  <Fragment slot="content">{fr ? <><h2>Qu'est-ce que les paramètres UTM et pourquoi les utiliser ?</h2><p>Les paramètres UTM (Urchin Tracking Module) sont des balises ajoutées à la fin de vos URL. Quand quelqu'un clique sur un lien avec des paramètres UTM, ces balises sont envoyées à Google Analytics pour un suivi précis.</p><h3>Paramètres expliqués</h3><ul><li><strong>Source</strong> : l'origine de votre trafic (google, newsletter, facebook).</li><li><strong>Média</strong> : le canal marketing (cpc, email, social).</li><li><strong>Campagne</strong> : le nom de votre campagne spécifique (ex. summer_sale).</li></ul><p>Utiliser des UTM est essentiel pour comprendre quels liens génèrent du trafic et des ventes, et optimiser vos dépenses publicitaires.</p></> : <><h2>What are UTM parameters and why use them?</h2><p>UTM (Urchin Tracking Module) parameters are tags you add to the end of your URLs. When someone clicks a URL with UTM parameters, those tags are sent to Google Analytics for precise tracking.</p><h3>Parameters explained</h3><ul><li><strong>Source</strong>: the origin of your traffic (google, newsletter, facebook).</li><li><strong>Medium</strong>: the marketing medium (cpc, email, social).</li><li><strong>Campaign</strong>: the name of your specific campaign (e.g. summer_sale).</li></ul><p>Using UTMs is essential to understand which links drive traffic and sales, allowing you to optimize your ad spend.</p></>}</Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
